      "writtenOn": "2019-08-08T22:01:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit: naming\nIt\u0027s often better to have context in the function name itself, and then the arguments can be shorter.\n\nFor example:\n\nvoid fp_disable_positive_match_secret(struct fp_match_secret *secret);\n\nSince the argument name is typically used inside the function where context is clear it\u0027s not necessary to repeat the context every time so the argument can have more concise names. On the other hand it\u0027s nice to have a clear function name. Does that make sense?\n\nEDIT: I see you already applied that logic to the header :-)",
      "range": {
