      "writtenOn": "2019-08-13T18:30:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think in biod we use 32-bits a lot, for example in https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2/+/a41075df8b2723a25065b2af539d670ae0aed5cf/biod/cros_fp_device.cc#466 and https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2/+/a41075df8b2723a25065b2af539d670ae0aed5cf/biod/cros_fp_biometrics_manager.cc#554 for the dirty list and dirty bitmap, and https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2/+/a41075df8b2723a25065b2af539d670ae0aed5cf/biod/cros_fp_biometrics_manager.cc#572 which results from our macro pattern,\na cast is unavoidable even if I change this to uint16_t. I chose 8 bits mainly because I could save some (tiny) amount of time and resource in communication. I could change to uint8_t though, since this should never be negative. Unless we would use \"read secret for finger -1\" to represent some special meaning? I can\u0027t think of a use case.",
      "parentUuid": "26e63038_34e89906",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5741,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 5741,
