        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-08-14T22:35:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, biod does use 32-bit values a lot. I was hoping maybe we could fix biod at some point to be consistent, but I haven\u0027t looked through it enough to see whether it would be possible. It\u0027s always easy to change biod, but the EC commands have to be versioned (or we force a firmware update at the same time as biod), so it would be nice to not have to change in the future if we don\u0027t have to.\n\nI can\u0027t think of a use-case for negative value. We could always treat UINT8_MAX as special if we need to.",
